40, "time": "01:29:00", "artist": "Donald Banks", "title": "Status Quo", "conf": "high", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Donald+Banks+Status+Quo", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Donald+Banks+Status+Quo", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Donald+Banks+Status+Quo", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Donald+Banks+Status+Quo", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Donald+Banks+Status+Quo", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Donald+Banks+Status+Quo", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Donald+Banks+Status+Quo&type=all", "search": true}, {"label": "shazam", "url": "https://www.shazam.com/track/62006061", "search": false}], "notes": []}, {"t": 5623, "time": "01:33:43", "artist": "Jestofunk", "title": "The Ghetto", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Jestofunk+The+Ghetto", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Jestofunk+The+Ghetto", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Jestofunk+The+Ghetto", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Jestofunk+The+Ghetto", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Jestofunk+The+Ghetto", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Jestofunk+The+Ghetto", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Jestofunk+The+Ghetto&type=all", "search": true}, {"label": "shazam", "url": "https://www.shazam.com/track/91189125", "search": false}], "notes": ["1996 Irma Records"]}, {"t": 6072, "time": "01:41:12", "artist": "Soweto Gospel Choir & Groove Terminator", "title": "Ride Like The Wind (Latroit Edit)", "conf": "high", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Soweto+Gospel+Choir+%26+Groove+Terminator+Ride+Like+The+Wind+%28Latroit+Edit%29", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Soweto+Gospel+Choir+%26+Groove+Terminator+Ride+Like+The+Wind+%28Latroit+Edit%29", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Soweto+Gospel+Choir+%26+Groove+Terminator+Ride+Like+The+Wind+%28Latroit+Edit%29", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Soweto+Gospel+Choir+%26+Groove+Terminator+Ride+Like+The+Wind+%28Latroit+Edit%29", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Soweto+Gospel+Choir+%26+Groove+Terminator+Ride+Like+The+Wind+%28Latroit+Edit%29", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Soweto+Gospel+Choir+%26+Groove+Terminator+Ride+Like+The+Wind+%28Latroit+Edit%29", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Soweto+Gospel+Choir+%26+Groove+Terminator+Ride+Like+The+Wind+%28Latroit+Edit%29&type=all", "search": true}, {"label": "shazam", "url": "https://www.shazam.com/track/703704491", "search": false}], "notes": ["2024 Music Is Fun"]}, {"t": 6420, "time": "01:47:00", "artist": "One Way", "title": "You Can Do It (feat. Al Hudson) [12\" Version]", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=One+Way+You+Can+Do+It+%28feat.+Al+Hudson%29+%5B12%22+Version%5D", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=One+Way+You+Can+Do+It+%28feat.+Al+Hudson%29+%5B12%22+Version%5D", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=One+Way+You+Can+Do+It+%28feat.+Al+Hudson%29+%5B12%22+Version%5D", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/One+Way+You+Can+Do+It+%28feat.+Al+Hudson%29+%5B12%22+Version%5D", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=One+Way+You+Can+Do+It+%28feat.+Al+Hudson%29+%5B12%22+Version%5D", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/One+Way+You+Can+Do+It+%28feat.+Al+Hudson%29+%5B12%22+Version%5D", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=One+Way+You+Can+Do+It+%28feat.+Al+Hudson%29+%5B12%22+Version%5D&type=all", "search": true}, {"label": "shazam", "url": "https://www.shazam.com/track/60166600", "search": false}], "notes": ["1979 Geffen"]}, {"t": 6830, "time": "01:53:50", "artist": "Aretha Franklin", "title": "Get It Right", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Aretha+Franklin+Get+It+Right", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Aretha+Franklin+Get+It+Right", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Aretha+Franklin+Get+It+Right", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Aretha+Franklin+Get+It+Right", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Aretha+Franklin+Get+It+Right", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Aretha+Franklin+Get+It+Right", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Aretha+Franklin+Get+It+Right&type=all", "search": true}, {"label": "shazam", "url": "https://www.shazam.com/track/441737", "search": false}], "notes": ["1983 Arista"]}, {"t": 6968, "time": "01:56:08", "artist": "Khruangbin & Natasha Diggs", "title": "First Class (Soul in the Horn Remix)", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Khruangbin+%26+Natasha+Diggs+First+Class+%28Soul+in+the+Horn+Remix%29", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Khruangbin+%26+Natasha+Diggs+First+Class+%28Soul+in+the+Horn+Remix%29", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Khruangbin+%26+Natasha+Diggs+First+Class+%28Soul+in+the+Horn+Remix%29", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Khruangbin+%26+Natasha+Diggs+First+Class+%28Soul+in+the+Horn+Remix%29", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Khruangbin+%26+Natasha+Diggs+First+Class+%28Soul+in+the+Horn+Remix%29", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Khruangbin+%26+Natasha+Diggs+First+Class+%28Soul+in+the+Horn+Remix%29", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Khruangbin+%26+Natasha+Diggs+First+Class+%28Soul+in+the+Horn+Remix%29&type=all", "search": true}, {"label": "shazam", "url": "https://www.shazam.com/track/571967845", "search": false}], "notes": ["2021 Dead Oceans"]}], "counts": {"high": 17, "mid": 7, "low": 2}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:14:16", "end": "00:15:45", "text": "And that's Sounds of Blackness, put together by Jimmy Jam, Terry Lewis and Gary Hines from their album Time for Healing. I think it was his second, maybe third album, top of my head, 1998. Royalty is the tune there, featuring a special guest there, HSRA, Sounds of Blackness. And they actually took it to the charts. You know, they got gospel and they released a 45-piece vocal outfit. Jimmy Jam, Terry Lewis doing the production. I mean, you can't go too far wrong, can you? And absolutely solid gold American stuff. Thank you for sticking with us The very top there we had You Plus Me Equals Love Of 1976 Norman Whitfield The producer Who sort of went Off I guess Paddock You know Just to create Some really different tunes there And he wrote And produced that particular tune for And I think it was a group Put together by him The Undisputed Truth And Tucker Boom Was the singer As mentioned Sister of Chaka Khan And he did make the charts The Disco Chart 37 Pop Charts 48 UK Top 50 as well And that was nearly The full version I don't think I've ever paid the full sort of 11 minutes long. It's quite a thing to hear in a club when it gets going and people start absolutely sort of adoring it and it just goes and goes and goes. Thanks for your company, FBI. This is sold out. Next up is a tune from, and it's one of my all-time favorites. I used to play back in the 90s at the Blue Room, Grand Pacific Blue Room, from Maloko. This is a track that comes from the album, Do You Like My Sweater? Do You Like My Sweater? Mark Brydon, Roshin Murphy, of course, and their earlier years, and this track is called Fun For Me. Amen."}, {"start": "00:24:13", "end": "00:25:08", "text": "It was criticised by a number of purists, of course, in the jazz format, but turning from a jazz virtuoso into a global superstar. That track, Breezin, came from a track by Tommy La Puma from the album Breezin. And 1971, well, 71 was originally done by Bobby Womack, I should say, and then this came a little bit later. I'm trying to think of the time frame. But it's a sample by Sound Unlimited Posse, of course, locally. Breezin, George Benson. Before that, we had Maloko in the early days, 1995, I think, no, no, 998. Fun for me was the tune, and they put together that slightly surreal sort of lyric cover. The whole thing was sort of quirky, classic Roshin and Murphy, and put together Mark Brydon there at a time, I suppose, where Trip Hop was really starting to cut through big time. This is Sold Out, Stephen Ferris with you. Let's go with Brand. She's really at the singles, a brand new one from Chaka Khan."}, {"start": "00:38:46", "end": "00:40:18", "text": "Extended rework there. That's an M2M8 track from 1980. So you want to be a star. From the album In Search of the Rainbow Seekers, James M2M8, Reggie Lucas, of course, put it together. Lead vocals by Tawatha Aguirre. I think Tawatha used to sing with Sheep from memory. This is sold out. It's around about 5.39. Stephen Ferris with you. No soul scape tonight. Swedish Fish is moving house. Hopefully for the better. And we should be back soon. So before MJ was Dave Lee, along with singer Omar, you know that voice, Starlight's the tune. Pretty much a couple of years ago, the very top there. I'm confused with this on Chaka Khan. She's got an album out called Chuck Zilla. And Chuck Zilla is brand new, and that track features on that album. Though I think it's been in the wash for a year or two anyway. Mark Ronson produced and wrote that track. Curious subject, Chaka Khan. It's got a nice sort of bouncing boogie feel to it. You'll tune to FBI 94.5, of course. FBI.radio, you can stream and follow more. I haven't actually written up the tracks yet, but we'll get to that at some point. This next track comes from a local artist, Miss Canina, and brand new from the EP slash mixtape Blackprint, and it's just got me completely besotted. I think it's the 90s feel. You'll hear it when I play it. You'll hear what I'm talking about, and put together with 80-year-old man and Ethan Parody, Miss Canina, and try it cold."}, {"start": "00:48:44", "end": "00:49:13", "text": "And of course, yeah, it's a very, very strong, fierce political anthem and very sexual in content as well about global black solidarity, et cetera, et cetera. I love it to death. It's called Mob Ties. Miss Canina there with Blackprint, the EP that's out or the mix tape, whatever you want to call it. You rock my world, Michael Jackson, Invincible, which is the album, 2001. You are on FBi 94.5. It is 10 minutes to six. Stephen Ferris with you."}, {"start": "01:02:03", "end": "01:02:33", "text": "The album came out in 1992 but that song came out in 1990 with great references to the Rolling Stones and is that a Moog or is it a Clavinet put through some sort of you know I don't know but I love it and it was a big play back in the bars particularly in the clubs that play slower tempo stuff and talking slow tempo the song before it was done by Jazzy B and Nelly Hooper from Soul to Soul who really invented the slow groove at that time."}, {"start": "01:02:52", "end": "01:03:39", "text": "I think that was the lead single. Heaven was the one that followed not long after it. So going back in time, the very top there was the Eyes of Your Brothers from 1971, so that's a different groove altogether. Love the One You're With. Stephen Sills did it in the year before, 1970, wrote it, produced it, sang it, and then the Eyes of Your Brothers picked it up and giving it back was the album from 71, Love the One You're With. It's pretty well known these days as one of those sort of classic sort of soft rock crossover, yacht rock-y sort of genre sort of tracks, but it's way beyond that, way above that. And one, two, three in the middle. The Chimes, The Master Plan, Diana Brown and Barry K. Sharp. This next track goes out to my friend Panda. Strong music by Gil Scott Heron from the album Reflections. Hope she likes it."}, {"start": "01:10:44", "end": "01:13:12", "text": "And they will come, of course, many, many, many, one of those golden American classics that everybody's covered from Cher to the Supremes, Isaac Hayes, I think Frank Sinatra, Tony Bennett, Diane Warwick, The Carpenters, and originally done by Ruby and the Romantics back in 62, but that was the amazing and late Amy Winehouse there. This is sold out Stephen First with you till 7pm It is now 11 minutes after 6 Before that we had Gil Scott Herum That one went out to Panda Special request Storm Music From the album Reflections from 1981 Obviously in America And I was there in 80 onwards And I'd seen Bob Marley perform before that in Australia And obviously reggae and Bob Marley Had infused many many cultures around the world But it took a long while A slow crawl to creep through American Sort of stylistic things I mean the Stones had a crack at it You know blah blah blah But that was Gil Scott Heron with a whole reggae sort of tinge to that particular tune Hope you're enjoying the tunes There is a text on 0435 123 945 And I'm just starting to look for it now George Jordan Breezen Yeah, yeah, 75 for George Yeah, fantastic So feel free, feel free We have another party, Sold Out has another party Which is happening on November the 8th And I'm hoping, I'm hoping that You know, you might want to consider coming There's an early bird ticket sale which is sort of reaching conclusion pretty soon. And it's me, Josh Beagley, the godfather, Swedish Fish, who is not here tonight, but she'll be there on the night, but she'll be there on other Sundays. But on November 8th, special guest DJ Groove Terminator, now based in the Northern Rivers area, but originally from Adelaide. And good old running mate of Josh Beagley and a man who knew the funk and the beats, et cetera, way back in the day. And he's going to do a special set for us. It'll be live to web, 5 to 7, starting at 2 o'clock till 8 p.m. National Arts. We're back there. we've been away for quite a while now at the Paddo RSL and there's an early bird ticket going at Flickit Flickit's the place to go or if you go to the sold out underscore Australia Instagram page you can find in the link there there's a ticket link but you can find just go to Flickit sold out number 8 it's called sold out 8 myself Stephen Ferris that's me Josh Beagley the Godfather Swedish Fish and DJ Groove Terminator special guest for that particular night presented by National Art School and FBI Radio so keep that on board And early tickets are very strong at the moment So I hope you can consider if you love the show What am I going to play now? Of course, I love playing a little bit of James Brown"}, {"start": "01:23:43", "end": "01:25:33", "text": "KC, otherwise known as KC, and Richard Finch, KC, and the Sunshine Band. But that's Jimmy Bell Horne, who was one of the go-to singers that they produced in the day. The songs were sort of into, you could replace one singer with another, and it would still do the job. Such a classic hit-making ability, and the funky blues that KC and the Sunshine Band could pull off. Nothing, nothing, nothing, no dirt on them, and their incredible sort of outfit. And that's one of those tracks that's been sampled. I think Stereo Home Season might have got their hands on at some point. Not that it gives credibility. I'm telling you that for nothing. For that James Brown, that was the lead singles before the Payback album in 1973, Stone to the Bone. That's the original long version. He often did that, James Brown, just to put it over the A side and the B side of his seven-inch singles at the time until it hit the album. And then it was usually a double album, the Payback, and extraordinary funk, just solid, the best ground zero funk. James Brown. And, of course, that had the all-star cast there with the JBs, Fred Wesley, Maceo Parker, John Jabbo Sparks on drums Fred Thomas on bass line and amongst many others and Stone to the Bone what's it about? I don't know doesn't matter it's James Brown really doesn't matter at all and what else was it we had Amy Winehouse of course if you missed that this is sold out it is 624 I'll have a look at the text in a minute the number is 0435123945 yes November 8 hold the date for sold out 8 it's our next party happening at the National Arts School from 2 o'clock in the afternoon 5 we go live to air till 7 as we do here on a Sunday it's a Sunday beautiful afternoon in November in sort of approaching summer and then finish at 8 o'clock special guest Groove Terminator tickets now available at Flicket and Early Bird is running out very fast so hopefully if you're inclined get amongst it Leon Haywood Disco Fever have I got it? I got it"}, {"start": "01:40:33", "end": "01:41:14", "text": "The producer of that one was Nature's Creation. Don't you love that one? And, yeah, that was Status Quo, Donald Banks. At the very top there, Leon Hayward, a l